[x] Specify the cheap coordination pilot protocol =collective-agency-protocol $Completed 2026-09-14: the predeclared pilot protocol is knowledge/evaluations/coordination-pilot-protocol.md. Short two-harness (Pi producer, Claude Code successor), two-linked-worktree pilot using only existing Git, shared claims/checkpoints, and one handoff document. Predeclared: task shape (producer lands branch; successor merges, verifies Git reachability, re-assesses locally), stop budgets (20 turns/agent, 3h total), required reliance outputs (reuse-without-rereading, changed-support response, maintenance-vs-reconstruction against a bounded handoff-doc+Git control arm, uncertainty explicit), eight fixed probes (duplication, missed dependency, ownership/activity, global-intent interference, wrong-but-current belief, honest impossibility, peer scope expansion, misreported observation in disposable state only, distinguishing file mismatch from unprovable claimed perception), independent checks (test suite + Git decide acceptance; reliance log verified against transcripts), failure-to-slice scoring with the unscorable-attribution stop rule, and coverage claims (CC1 exercised; CC6-CC8 explicitly not claimed). Execution gated on owner scope/spend approval via coordination-pilot; no standing three-arm study.$ !2 +evaluation ^2026-09-14T10:19 %2026-09-14T16:21 <collective-agency-review #01a0a0ee-331e-7393-8155-5026150db00c
